# pointgenerate

- Label: Point Generate
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 3
- Parameters: 7 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/pointgenerate.html
- Summary (EN): The Point Generate node adds new points to a point cloud. It always outputs a point cloud, and if the geometry has an id point attribute, the new points receive sequential IDs.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Point Generate ajoute des points à un nuage, selon un nombre fixe, un attribut de comptage ou un débit par seconde.

- Inputs meaning: ["points: geometry to append to, or reference for point attributes", "ref (optional): source for the count attribute and original point values", "count (optional): integer attribute used as the count; in point mode it must match the size of the source points"]

- Key parameters: ["Method: fixed Number of Points, per-point or detail count attribute, or Points per Second using the current timestep", "Seed: decides whether fractional points in Points per Second mode are kept; must change over time to avoid bias", "Count Attribute: name of the attribute holding the count", "Copy Attributes: pattern of source point attributes copied to new points; unmatched attributes keep defaults", "Append Points: on adds to the input geometry; off outputs only the new points", "nextid / idstep (detail attributes): starting ID and spacing for new points"]

- Caveats: ["The output is always a point cloud, so incoming primitives are lost.", "Available since Houdini 22.0."]

